<title>ITALY: Italy industrial orders down 3.7 pct yr-yr in Jan.</title>
<headline>Italy industrial orders down 3.7 pct yr-yr in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian industrial orders fell 3.7 percent year-on-year in January while turnover fell 3.9 percent, national statistics institute Istat said.  </p>
<p>    INDUSTRIAL ORDERS     Jan 1997     Dic 1996     Jan 1996</p>
<p>    Year on year change  -3.7 pct	-5.9 pct     +1.0 pct</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     133.9	   137.7	  139.1</p>
<p>    -Domestic demand     -6.9 pct	-8.9	   +1.3 pct</p>
<p>    -Foreign demand	+1.1 pct	-1.0	   +0,5 pct</p>
<p>INDUSTRIAL TURNOVER</p>
<p>    Year on year change  -3.9 pct	+0.6 pct     +8.9 pct</p>
<p>    Index (100= 1990)     123.2	  146.1	   128.2</p>
<p>    -Domestic demand     -3.1 pct	-1.4 pct     +7.1 pct</p>
<p>    -Foreign demand	-5.5 pct	+5.7 pct     +13.2 pct</p>
<p>Note: Istat said the increase in turnover was especially marked in the mining sector where sales climbed 11.2 percent. Sales fell 14.2 percent in the metal industries sector.</p>
<p>For orders there was a 12.7 percent increase in demand for mechanical machinery.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
